/T (For the OOM issue, PHP describes administratively enforcing memory_limit=-1 as a partial measure. It removes the predictable PHP memory-limit trigger, but underlying allocation failures can still reach vulnerable behavior. Removing the cap also increases memory-exhaustion risk. )
