<<
/Title (PHP has released emergency updates for CVE-2026-109618 and CVE-2026-109619, two critical vulnerabilities known as PHP2Shell. Successful exploitation can allow an unauthenticated attacker to execute code with the privileges of the PHP web worker.)
/Dest [11 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 520 0 R
/Next 635 0 R
>>
endobj
635 0 obj
<<
/Title (The PHP team urges administrators to update affected installations immediately. Apache with mod_php is considered the highest-risk configuration because demonstrated attacks can reach vulnerable code before the requested application script starts running. Fixed versions are listed on page 6.)
